@gateway = http://localhost:8080

# Everything goes through the gateway on 8080. The services still listen on their own
# ports on a dev machine, but nothing here needs them except the defence-in-depth check
# in the last section.
#
# Seeded dev accounts:
#   alice@orqentra.test / alice-pass  -> RESTAURANT, Alice Trattoria
#   bob@orqentra.test   / bob-pass    -> RESTAURANT, Bob Bistro
#   admin@orqentra.test / admin-pass  -> ADMIN
#
# The saga resolves asynchronously: a POST returns PENDING and a GET straight after may
# still show PENDING or AWAITING_PAYMENT. Re-run the GET to see the final state.

### ==================== Auth ====================

### Log in as restaurant A (Alice)
# @name login
POST {{gateway}}/api/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "alice@orqentra.test",
  "password": "alice-pass"
}

### Log in as restaurant B (Bob)
# @name loginB
POST {{gateway}}/api/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "bob@orqentra.test",
  "password": "bob-pass"
}

### Log in as the admin
# @name loginAdmin
POST {{gateway}}/api/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "admin@orqentra.test",
  "password": "admin-pass"
}

### Register a new restaurant
POST {{gateway}}/api/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "dave@orqentra.test",
  "password": "dave-pass",
  "restaurantName": "Dave Diner"
}

### Who am I
GET {{gateway}}/api/auth/me
Authorization: Bearer {{login.response.body.$.token}}

### ==================== Rejected at the edge ====================

### No token -> 401 ProblemDetail, from the gateway. Never reaches the order service.
GET {{gateway}}/api/orders

### Malformed token -> 401 ProblemDetail, from the gateway
GET {{gateway}}/api/orders
Authorization: Bearer not-a-real-token

### RESTAURANT token on an admin route -> 403 at the edge
GET {{gateway}}/api/admin/dlq/topics
Authorization: Bearer {{login.response.body.$.token}}

### CORS preflight. Expect exactly one Access-Control-Allow-Origin header.
OPTIONS {{gateway}}/api/orders
Origin: http://localhost:5173
Access-Control-Request-Method: POST
Access-Control-Request-Headers: authorization,content-type

### ==================== The saga, through the gateway ====================

### Stock before, SKU-001
GET {{gateway}}/api/inventory/SKU-001
Authorization: Bearer {{login.response.body.$.token}}

### Place a small order. X-Request-Id is echoed back and follows the saga into Kafka.
# @name smallOrder
POST {{gateway}}/api/orders
Authorization: Bearer {{login.response.body.$.token}}
Content-Type: application/json
X-Request-Id: demo-request-0001

{
  "items": [
    { "sku": "SKU-001", "quantity": 2 }
  ]
}

### Read it back -> CONFIRMED
GET {{gateway}}/api/orders/{{smallOrder.response.body.$.reference}}
Authorization: Bearer {{login.response.body.$.token}}

### Stock reduced by 2
GET {{gateway}}/api/inventory/SKU-001
Authorization: Bearer {{login.response.body.$.token}}

### Payment record -> SUCCEEDED
GET {{gateway}}/api/payments/{{smallOrder.response.body.$.reference}}
Authorization: Bearer {{login.response.body.$.token}}

### This restaurant's own orders
GET {{gateway}}/api/orders?page=0&size=10
Authorization: Bearer {{login.response.body.$.token}}

### ==================== Compensation ====================

### Large order (62500, over the decline threshold)
# @name largeOrder
POST {{gateway}}/api/orders
Authorization: Bearer {{login.response.body.$.token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "items": [
    { "sku": "SKU-001", "quantity": 5 }
  ]
}

### Read it back -> CANCELLED, "Amount exceeds card limit"
GET {{gateway}}/api/orders/{{largeOrder.response.body.$.reference}}
Authorization: Bearer {{login.response.body.$.token}}

### Stock back to its pre-order level
GET {{gateway}}/api/inventory/SKU-001
Authorization: Bearer {{login.response.body.$.token}}

### ==================== Cross-tenant ====================

### Bob asks for Alice's order -> 404, not 403
GET {{gateway}}/api/orders/{{smallOrder.response.body.$.reference}}
Authorization: Bearer {{loginB.response.body.$.token}}

### ==================== Admin ====================

### Dead letter topics with an ADMIN token -> 200
GET {{gateway}}/api/admin/dlq/topics
Authorization: Bearer {{loginAdmin.response.body.$.token}}

### Messages in a dead letter topic
GET {{gateway}}/api/admin/dlq/order.created.dlq
Authorization: Bearer {{loginAdmin.response.body.$.token}}

### Stuck orders
GET {{gateway}}/api/admin/stuck-orders
Authorization: Bearer {{loginAdmin.response.body.$.token}}

### ==================== Rate limit ====================

# Configured at ~5/sec with a burst of 10. Send this repeatedly in quick succession and
# it turns into a 429 ProblemDetail once the bucket empties.
GET {{gateway}}/api/inventory/SKU-001
Authorization: Bearer {{login.response.body.$.token}}

### Login is rate limited by client IP, since there is no identity to key on yet
POST {{gateway}}/api/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "alice@orqentra.test",
  "password": "alice-pass"
}

### ==================== Live updates (SSE) ====================

# The stream stays open: REST Client shows events as they arrive and the request never
# completes. Stop it manually. To watch it in a terminal instead, run watch-stream.ps1,
# which uses curl.exe -N so output is not buffered.
#
# The restaurant is taken from the token, never from a query parameter, so a client can
# only ever receive its own orders. An ADMIN token subscribes to every restaurant.
#
# Event names are what the client cares about (order.status, stock.released), not the
# internal topic names, so the browser is not coupled to the saga's decomposition.

### Subscribe to the live order stream
GET {{gateway}}/api/notifications/stream
Authorization: Bearer {{login.response.body.$.token}}
Accept: text/event-stream

### Subscribe with no token -> 401 at the gateway
GET {{gateway}}/api/notifications/stream
Accept: text/event-stream

### Subscribe as the admin -> receives every restaurant's events
GET {{gateway}}/api/notifications/stream
Authorization: Bearer {{loginAdmin.response.body.$.token}}
Accept: text/event-stream

### Open connections and known order mappings
GET {{gateway}}/api/notifications/stats
Authorization: Bearer {{login.response.body.$.token}}

### ==================== Direct to service: defence in depth only ====================

# These bypass the gateway deliberately. On a dev machine the services are reachable on
# their own ports; in a real deployment they would sit on an internal network with only
# the gateway exposed. Either way each service verifies the JWT itself, so an invalid
# token is refused here too.

### Invalid token straight to the order service on 8084 -> must still be 401
GET http://localhost:8084/api/orders
Authorization: Bearer not-a-real-token

### Valid token straight to the order service -> 200, the service trusts the token, not the caller
GET http://localhost:8084/api/orders
Authorization: Bearer {{login.response.body.$.token}}
